  "$comment": "Where a fish lives in the wild, as a species page will show it (no block is drawn yet: web and iOS come after the owner's review), and the words the app names its countries with. The content's `range` (packages/schema/src/schemas.ts RangeSchema; written by the engine, packages/engine/src/range.ts) becomes a fish's app index entry's `range` through appRange (apps/site/src/lib/range.ts); the app reads that entry as it is and never sees the content. apps/site/test/range-vectors.test.ts holds this file to the site: each case's `entry` is appRange's for its `range`; a `species` case's range is the fixture content's (apps/site/test/fixture-content) and its entry the fixture build's app index's; `countries` is that index's names for the real cases' countries; `names` is each country's name in vi, id, th and en from Intl.DisplayNames. UPDATE_VECTORS=1 pnpm --filter site test rewrites the file: edit only the notes, the made-up ranges and the `species` ids. `range` (content): `native`, present when the species' sources name where it lives: `countries`, ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 codes in the order the sources name them, each from a sentence of a cited source that names the country (kept in engine-state/range/<id>.json), none a source calls introduced or doubtful; `regions`, river systems, lakes, islands and wider natural regions as the sources write them, at most 6; `sources`, the source ids they come from. `records`, present once fetched: the species' wild records on GBIF (taxon `taxonKey`; occurrence status present, coordinates without geospatial issues, no living or fossil specimens, licence CC0 or CC BY 4.0, never NC) counted on `fetched` (YYYY-MM-DD): `total`; `countries`, [code, records] by GBIF's country field, most first then by code (a record at sea or with no country is in `total` only); `cells`, [west, south, records] or, when there are native countries, [west, south, records, of them in a native country]: the 1.40625° squares of GBIF's map that hold any, edges in degrees (a cell on a border can hold both). The cells add up to `total` and their inside counts to the native countries' records. `entry` (the index, AppItem.range): none when the range has neither part. `native`, the codes, when there are any; `regions`, each in the page's language where the site has a place of that name (its river or region page's name), else as written; `records`: `total`, `taxonKey`, `fetched`, and, only when there are native countries, `inside` (the native countries' records) and `outside` (the 5 other countries with the most records, [code, records], most first then by code; [] when none). No cells: the map that will draw them reads the content. Each code in an entry is named in the index's `countries` ({code: {name, place?}}, A to Z, only codes some entry names): the site's country page's name in that language where it has one, with `place`, its origin page's id among the index's `places`, else Intl.DisplayNames' name. The credit for records reads \"GBIF.org, <total> records, CC BY 4.0\", with the day they were counted.",
